From f500f0dea1a197727da1249642ef33079efe423e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:24:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: don't start the DPTX endpoint for internal panels

On the M4 MacBook Air (J713) the internal eDP panel is driven through
the DPTX PHY, so the DCP node needs the PHY (phy_init/phy_power_on at
probe); without it the panel stays dark with the backlight on, the DCP
reports DPTX FIFO errors and crashes touching the unpowered PHY on
power-off. With a 'phys' property the driver also assumes an external
DP port and waits for dcpdptx-port services, but the firmware runs the
internal panel as disp0 and never offers them, so the wait times out
(-110) on every boot. Skip dptxep_init() when the DCP drives a panel.

dcp->dptxep then stays NULL and dptxport[0].enabled false, as on
panel boots without a PHY, and every other user checks those first.

[Youwes09: from niklassheth/linux 7e86205e233d]
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index be83e7d4f3c5..615264e70b2b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -1146,7 +1146,13 @@ int dcp_start(struct platform_device *pdev)
 						     "Failed to start EPIC25 endpoint\n");
 		}
 
-		ret = dptxep_init(dcp);
+		/*
+		 * An internal eDP panel driven through the DPTX PHY (M4 MacBook
+		 * Air) needs the PHY powered, but its firmware runs the panel as
+		 * disp0 and offers no dcpdptx-port services: waiting for them
+		 * only times out.
+		 */
+		ret = dcp_has_panel(dcp) ? 0 : dptxep_init(dcp);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_warn(dcp->dev, "Failed to start DPTX endpoint: %d\n",
 				 ret);
